## **6. Step-by-Step Debugging Workflow**

| Step | Action | Tool/Command | What to Look For |
|------|--------|--------------|------------------|
| 1 | Enable JVM network logging | `-Djavax.net.debug=all` | HTTP/HTTPS errors, payloads |
| 2 | Enable Spring HTTP logging | `logging.level.org.springframework.web.client=DEBUG` | Request/response details |
| 3 | Add a `RestTemplate` interceptor | Custom Java code | vRA API request/response bodies |
| 4 | Use a proxy (Fiddler/Charles) | `-Dhttp.proxyHost=127.0.0.1 -Dhttp.proxyPort=8888` | Failed requests, payloads |
| 5 | Capture raw traffic | `tcpdump` or Wireshark | TCP resets, HTTP errors |
| 6 | Check vRA logs | `/var/log/vmware/vcac/` | Server-side refusals |

